                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Absolutely incredible game. Hilarious weird and interesting throughout. Unfortunately it is also a pain to play nowadays with dosbox. The default steam version works fine for the most part, but has an issue where it will skip most cutscenes. Tinkering with cycles did not result in any difference personally, though others have seemingly had success with this method. The beta build fixes this problem, but introduces a new problem where every time you have to kill, or choose to kill, an NPC with dialogue the game immediately crashes. This resulted in me having to switch back and forth from the default build to the beta build and vice versa to get around crashes and also be able to see the cutscenes. Far from an ideal experience and if it wasnt for the fact that I was loving the game so much I would have dropped it. This will, very understandably, be a dealbreaker for people so be warned before jumping in. However I just can't bring myself to give this a non-positive rating as it was such a unique and enjoyable game despite these annoyances.",
